summary: 'Began actually building Loom on branch loom-engine (off main). Phase-1 discipline (per TD-2026-06-23-398 roadmap + Jinx''s accepted proof): build the CONVERGENCE/DIVERGENCE ORACLE first — read-only on git (zero data-loss risk), runs on THIS repo''s real branches immediately, and forces building the real primitives (WARP store, ABSORB, the Justification, the meaning-diff) along the way. If meaning carries merge-information bytes can''t, the Oracle proves it with data; if not, we learn cheaply. WARP v0 granularity = the Paradigm symbol graph made content-addressed (reuse premise-core aggregateFromDirectory + buildSymbolIndex + the related[] edges as ABSORB; ripple for blast-radius). The Oracle: ABSORB two branches + their merge-base → meaning-deltas per branch → predict merge outcome (clean / knot / dangling) → run git''s actual merge → score convergence to a jsonl. The load-bearing hard part flagged 3x by the panel: the identity ''essence'' hash — hash the STRUCTURED contract (kind + normalized contract + edges-by-target-hash), NEVER embeddings, deterministic, rename-free. Architecture pass underway: Arky (engine + object model + Oracle flow + packages/loom layout), Cid (the essence hash + the SemDelta commute/knot/dangle algebra + determinism/cycle/aliasing handling).'
